# Git — Conventional Commits

All commits (API, web, root) use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/).

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <short description>

[optional body]
```

- **type**: `feat` | `fix` | `docs` | `style` | `refactor` | `test` | `chore` | `ci` | `build` | `perf`
- **scope**: `api` | `web` | `deps` | omit for repo-wide changes
- **description**: imperative, lowercase, no period at end (max ~72 chars)

## Examples

```
feat(web): add Button atom with primary variant
fix(api): return 404 when resource not found
test(web): cover SearchBar submit interaction
docs: document REST error response format
chore(deps): bump vite to 8.1
```

## Rules

- ✅ One logical change per commit; split if needed
- ✅ `test` type when commit is only tests; `feat`/`fix` include code + tests together when coupled
- ❌ Vague messages: `update`, `fix stuff`, `wip`
- ❌ Mix unrelated API and web changes in one commit unless truly atomic
